---
layout: layouts/base.njk
---
{#
  Article layout: the existing frame, plus a title, a byline and the body.
  Nothing else. This is step one of the article system and deliberately adds no
  chrome of its own.

  It chains to layouts/base.njk rather than restating the shell, which is how
  the five marketing pages already get the masthead, the colophon and the
  JSON-LD block. Nothing here rebuilds any of that.

  MEASURE. base/elements.css already caps p at 66ch, so paragraphs were at
  measure before this layout existed. Headings, lists, blockquotes and
  everything else were NOT: without a wrapper they would run the full 1120px of
  .cs-container while the paragraphs between them sat at 66ch, which reads as a
  broken column rather than a narrow one. So the cap belongs on the wrapper.

  max-w-measure is the utility --container-measure already generates, so this
  introduces no CSS. It also makes p's own 66ch redundant here, harmlessly: the
  two are the same value, and elements.css still needs its rule for prose that
  is not inside this layout.

  The <article> element is deliberate rather than reusing the section() macro,
  which emits <section>. Semantics are the point on a page that is one article.
#}
{#- The `header` field picks the title treatment (SHORTCODES.md: standard,
    feature, compact, cover, glyph). standard and feature share the base scale,
    so only compact and cover have rules; an unset field falls through to the
    base, which is what a piece with no opinion should get. -#}
<article class="cs-article py-24{{ " cs-article--" + header if header }}">
  <div class="cs-article__column cs-prose">
  {#- cover is the one header treatment that is a component rather than a
      scale. It replaces the standard header outright, carrying the kind, the
      title, the deck and the byline fields in its own panel, so nothing below
      is rendered twice. See partials/cover.njk. -#}
  {%- if header == "cover" %}
  {% include "partials/cover.njk" %}
  {%- else %}
  <header>
    <p class="caption">{{ kind }}</p>

    <h1>{{ title }}</h1>

    {% if deck %}<p class="cs-article__deck">{{ deck }}</p>{% endif %}

    {# author is a KEY per SHORTCODES.md, never a display name, and resolves
       against _data/authors.js. An unknown key falls back to the key itself
       rather than to nothing: a lowercase handle sitting in a byline is
       obviously wrong and greppable, whereas a blank byline reads as an
       article nobody wrote and could ship unnoticed. #}
    {%- set byline = authors[author] -%}
    {# The date is emitted twice on purpose: the visible string for a reader,
       and the machine date in datetime= for an answer engine deciding whether
       this piece is current. Both filters read UTC parts, so the two can never
       disagree by a day. #}
    <p class="caption">{{ byline.name if byline else author }}, updated
      <time datetime="{{ updated | isoDate }}">{{ updated | calendarDate }}</time></p>
  </header>
  {%- endif %}

  {{ content | safe }}
  </div>
</article>
